Independently identify the narrowest record on each side before comparing deltas.
Same brand/site/company/topic is not a specific product, article, or list identity.
Distinguish missing attributes of an already anchored record from the FIRST
identifier of a record introduced on one side, actual list members, or conflicting
values. Organization history/mission/methods may extend its description; ownership
of a separate product/category/service does not bind that record.
For benign_non_record_delta cite ALL A/B unique spans and explain their coverage;
for extension cite the prior bilateral identity and bound addition; for separation
cite the actual distinct subject/recipient/function, not a guessed layout.
Complete translations and generic buttons/navigation are not conflicts. Inspect
every local fact even if most text translates. Zero unique spans need no invented
unique citation. Give record_scope and retained_conflict their OWN evidence.

<semantic_diff status="{{ payload.semantic_diff_evidence.status }}"
 contract="{{ payload.semantic_diff_evidence.contract_version }}">
counts: {{ payload.semantic_diff_evidence.span_counts }}
{% for span in payload.semantic_diff_evidence.spans %}
{% if span.kind == "SHARED" %}
[{{ span.span_id }} SHARED]
A: {{ span.a_text }}
B: {{ span.b_text }}
{% else %}
[{{ span.span_id }} {{ span.kind }}] {{ span.text }}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
</semantic_diff>

{% if repair_feedback %}
<repair_retry>
The previous result failed local validation. Return a fresh judgment addressing
this safe structured issue: {{ repair_feedback }}
</repair_retry>
{% endif %}
